## Amount Conversion Helper

All SDK amounts use the **smallest currency unit** (cents for USD).

```kotlin
/** Convert dollars to cents for SDK AmountInfo */
fun dollarsToCents(dollars: Double): BigDecimal =
    BigDecimal(dollars).multiply(BigDecimal("100")).setScale(0, RoundingMode.HALF_UP)

/** Convert cents from SDK result back to dollars for display */
fun centsToDollars(cents: BigDecimal): BigDecimal =
    cents.divide(BigDecimal("100"), 2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP)
```

---

## Must-Follow Rules Summary

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Amount unit** | Always smallest currency unit (cents). `$10.00` → `BigDecimal("1000")` |
| **transactionRequestId** | Globally unique per attempt. Use `"TXN_${System.currentTimeMillis()}"` |
| **Error 306** | MUST query status before retrying. Transaction may have succeeded |
| **Lifecycle** | Call `disconnect()` + `removeConnectionListener()` in `onDestroy()` |
| **Thread safety** | Callbacks may arrive on background thread. Use `runOnUiThread {}` |
| **INIT session** | Auto-runs on first transaction after connect. No manual call needed |
| **Logs in production** | Set `logEnabled = false` to avoid leaking sensitive data |
